 "intro": [
  "The three Levite clans, Gershom, Kohath and Merari, first as descending lists (6:16–30), then as the ancestry of the three chief singers David appointed: Heman of Kohath in the centre, Asaph of Gershom at his right hand, Ethan of Merari on the left (6:31–47). The singers' lines are traced all the way back to Levi; the section ends with the priests from Aaron to Ahimaaz (6:49–53).",
  "The two kinds of list do not always agree in their names (Zophai and Zuph, Nahath and Toah, Eliab and Eliel), and some lists here are shown twice."
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah (Hebrew 6:1–38). Babylonian Talmud, Arakhin 11b and Taanit 5b; Rashi on 1 Chronicles 6. Psalms of Asaph (50; 73–83), Heman (88) and Ethan (89).",
 "anchor": {
